# Travel Map

This project generates an interactive map of cities using Python, [Folium](https://python-visualization.github.io/folium/), and [Geopy](https://geopy.readthedocs.io/). The map displays markers for each city listed in a text file, with detailed popups and marker clustering for easy exploration.

## Features

- Interactive map with modern CartoDB Positron tiles
- Marker clustering for dense areas
- Popups with detailed location info (address, etc.)
- Easy to use: just provide a text file with city names

## Requirements

- Python 3.8+
- [folium](https://pypi.org/project/folium/)
- [geopy](https://pypi.org/project/geopy/)

Install dependencies with:
```bash
pip install folium geopy
```

## Usage

1. **Prepare your cities file:**  
   Create a text file (e.g., `cities.txt`) with one city per line, e.g.:
   ```
   New York, NY
   San Francisco, CA
   Paris, France
   ```

2. **Run the script:**
   ```bash
   python create\ map.py
   ```
   When prompted, enter the full path to your `cities.txt` file.

3. **View your map:**  
   The script will generate `cities_map.html` in your project folder. Open it in your browser to explore your travel map!

